## Code provenance

The byte-level BPE tokenizer foundation was adapted from
[kimi-k3-in-c](https://github.com/FareedKhan-dev/kimi-k3-in-c), copyright
Fareed Khan and contributors, and is used under the Apache License 2.0. The
retained implementation is tailored to the Qwen tokenizer stored in GGUF.

The NFC normalization tables in `third_party/tok_nfc_data.h` are generated
from the Unicode 9.0.0 Character Database. The Unicode data license is
included in `third_party/UNICODE-LICENSE.txt`.

The native HTTP API uses `jsmn.h` from zserge/jsmn revision
`25647e692c7906b96ffd2b05ca54c097948e879c` under the MIT License, included in
`third_party/JSMN-LICENSE.txt`.

GGUF, the Q2_K through Q6_K and Q8_0/Q8_K encodings, and IQ tensor formats are
compatibility formats published by the ggml and llama.cpp projects. The fixed
IQ codebook tables in `third_party/ggml-common.h`, along with packed low-bit decoding and
kernel techniques used in `src/qwen38/qwen38_quant.c`, are adapted from ggml
revision `8c63e70982c95ceb862e3a1073a2c1beef75d60a` under its MIT license,
included as `third_party/GGML-LICENSE.txt`. The bounded GGUF parser, runtime
integration, row scheduling, and multi-token interfaces are project-local.
ggml and llama.cpp are not linked or invoked at runtime. A fixed llama.cpp
revision is also used as an external correctness oracle during validation.

The Qwen3.8 model graph, GGUF reader, quantized CPU kernels, batching,
recurrent state management, sampling, command-line runtime and MTP
verification in this repository are native project code. No external
inference engine is downloaded or invoked at runtime.

